course: dictionary
lesson: 10016
title: Temptation: wanting what you should not have
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Temptation is the feeling of wanting to do something, especially something you know is wrong or not good for you. «Charging devices outside the bedroom removes the temptation to play at night.» The sentence tells you the temptation is playing at night, and moving the devices away takes that wanting away.
explain: A temptation can also be a thing that makes you want to do something. «Cake is a big temptation» means cake makes it hard to stop yourself from eating it. Look for the phrases «resist temptation» (say no to it) and «give in to temptation» (say yes to it).
explain: Try the swap test. Put the word into a sentence about yourself: «My biggest temptation at bedtime is ...». If it fits, you have the right meaning. Then ask yourself: what do I want to do, and do I know it is wrong or not good for me?
fact: Temptation means a strong wish to do something you know is wrong or not good for you.
fact: A temptation can also be a thing that makes you want to do something, like cake.
fact: «Resist temptation» means to say no to it. «Give in to temptation» means you do it anyway.
fact: «A plan for the moment of temptation, such as a list of things to do when bored, helps habits change.»
fact: The Temptation, with a capital T, is also a story in religious teaching about Jesus being tempted by the devil in the desert.
exercise: «Charging devices outside the bedroom removes the temptation to play at night.» What is the temptation in this sentence? | Sleeping in late | Doing homework early | *Playing at night | Going to the shop
exercise: Maya says, «Cake is a big temptation.» What does she mean? | Cake is very good for your teeth | Cake is always made at home | *Cake makes it hard to stop yourself from eating it | Cake is free to eat
exercise: What does «resist temptation» mean? | To give in and do the wrong thing | *To say no to something you want but should not do | To go shopping for sweets | To forget that something exists
test: «Other friends met other temptations.» What are temptations in this sentence? | Friends who came to play | Good marks at school | Other people's birthday parties | *Things that made them want to do something they should not
test: What does «lead us not into temptation» ask for? | To go on a long trip | *To be kept away from things that would lead us to do wrong | To be the best at sport | To have more cake
exam: Which sentence shows the feeling of temptation? | Ellie went to bed early | Ben wrote a long story about dragons | *Tom wanted to take the sweets, even though his mum had said no | Sara found her lost cat under the bed
